Z||000001||Monkeyman||11-20-2001||04:44 PM||||I was under the impression that I could make the background disappear if I converted my Photoshopped image to a .GIF file.  Apparently I'm doing something wrong.  I tried.<p>[This message has been edited by Monkeyman (edited 11-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||DaRkLoRD||11-20-2001||05:14 PM||||with a GIF you can specify a color to be masked as transparent.. and everything in the image that is that color, is transparent. In photoshop, the easiest way is to use the eraser tool and delete the background. when this is exported as a gif, the transparent areas are translated to a color which web browsers read as invisible, hence the background "disappears".<P>btw, is that car from Canada?<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
